What’s something new you learned while building your site?:

 - That structure is not something you can pull sections of and call it good. you have to clean as you go otherwise things get lost, files cannot be recalled, and components won't activate 


How did you balance creativity with usability?:

 - I wanted to structure the posts as individual cards for people to look at so they could visually seperate each piece from the next one. Each body of work is a stand-alone project i worked on for hours and hours and I wanted people to get a sense of that visually so their eyes don't get crowded

What are you most proud of in your final project?:

 - That everything works and has continuity across the platform

How do you see yourself using these skills later on?:

 - The structure I was able to build is a "beta" for an actual website I want to produce. As
an artist I can't just bank on word-of-mouth, I have to advertise in the digital age. And if I can customize my website as something completely different than whatever platform everyone else uses (squarespace, no shade just obvious) then I can at least have a chance of catching the eye of anyone from any location. 